      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i am a freelance designer and im just trying to clean up my quickbooks before the end of the year. i bought a high end ergonomic office chair for my home studio like a few months ago. do i list that as a business expense or is that considered a personal draw? i am a bit confused on how to categorize equipment for my home office.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "As a freelance designer, you can generally deduct business expenses related to your home office, but personal expenses like a home office chair typically can't be deducted. You should separate your personal and business expenses on your QuickBooks. Consider setting up a home office as a separate entity or workspace within your business to streamline your accounting and potential tax deductions. It might also be useful to consult with a tax professional to clarify your specific situation and ensure compliance with tax laws.",
